      "question": {
        ":question/id": "57575c59-4fa1-5fb9-97ac-1738a281c256",
        ":question/problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{229}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{229}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{2}^{a}\\frac{229}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =229{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{2}^{a}{x}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =229{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[(-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-2})]}_{2}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{229}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}]}_{2}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{229}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{2}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{229}{2}(0-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{229}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "496008ee-9c09-5670-807c-ba80e7447bb4",
