        ":question/problem": "${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{586}{{\\theta }^{3}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta =$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{586}{{\\theta }^{3}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}\\frac{586}{{\\theta }^{3}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}586{\\theta }^{-3}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[(-293{\\theta }^{-2})]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-293\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{{\\theta }^{2}}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-293\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-293(0-1) \\\\  & =293.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
